  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nClosed upper high will linger over the northern high plains\nthrough Wednesday, keeping the heat going over the Dakotas and\ninto our SE zones through Wednesday. Will maintain Extreme Heat\nWarnings for Dawson, Richland, Prairie and Wibaux Counties where\nheat indices up to 110 is possible today and Heat Advisories for \nthe most of NE Montana except for Daniels and Sheridan Counties \ntoday. Then an upper disturbance sends storms northeast into the \nCWA this evening. Updraft helicity and Max Updraft from the HREF \nis showing severe thunderstorm potential for the western zones. \nWith the high Precip Waters (1.0 to 1.8\"), flooding could also be \na concern. Will maintain the Flash Flood Watch for the Petroleum \nand Phillips Counties for tonight.\n\nEast to NE winds will be strong enough today and tonight for a\nLake Wind Advisory over Fort Peck Lake.\n\nWednesday and beyond: Upper low over the Pacific NW then moves NE\ninto the Prairie Provinces of Canada while the upper ridge \nrebounds over eastern Montana. This should keep temps warmer than \nnormal with small chances for showers and storms.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nThere is high confidence in the heat continuing especially in the\nSE today and Wednesday. High confidence in thunderstorm chances in\nthe NW tonight but low confidence in timing and lower confidence\nfor thunderstorm chances for Wednesday and beyond. \n\nTweaked pops at times tonight and Wednesday to provide better hour\nto hour consistency. Otherwise, did not deviate from NBM.",
